\input{conditional_completion.tex}
\clearpage
\phantomsection
\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{References}
\input{references.tex}
\clearpage
\section{Worked visual atlas}\label{sec:atlas}
The following thirty pages reproduce the worked atlas from the separate visual
guide. They retain their own page labels Plates X.1--X.30, so the same example has the
same address in either reading route. The two opening contract pages of the
standalone guide are not repeated here.

The atlas develops exact finite models, not substitutes for universal proofs.
Its first part separates residual roots, coherent branches, and occupied carrier
packets. Its second part studies residue norms, cancellation, Mellin estimates,
and the boundary between a finite calculation and arithmetic occurrence.
The final page records the three distinct historical and current contracts.

The build script appends these source-built pages after this leaf and copies their
bookmarks and internal links. The mathematical manuscript, its historical
checkpoint statements, and the later conditional assembly remain above.
\end{document}

