\paragraph{Every required packet is necessary.}
For each omitted index $N\in\mathbb N$, consider one-dimensional rational carriers
with the identity operator, requiring eigenvalue $0$ at $N$ and eigenvalue $1$
at every other index. The actual spectral projector has trace $0$ at $N$ and
trace $1$ elsewhere. Lean proves that any predetermined finite sample of packet
indices can miss an empty required packet: choose $N$ outside that sample.
The family depends on the omitted index. This does not assert that one fixed
family passes every finite prefix while failing global occupancy.

\begin{conjecture}[Natural finite seed rank]\label{px:11.3}
For the admissible residual transport category attached to a fixed arithmetic class, the directed seed rank is finite.  A one-seed theorem additionally requires a source component from which every required object is reachable and transports preserving deformation and occupancy data.  For a finite condensation DAG, having exactly one source implies that reachability condition.  For an infinite category, the existence of a unique source alone does not establish it.
\end{conjecture}

