The source is \emph{Patching Support, Hecke Packets, and Conditional Automorphic Completion}, Komorebi P., revised formalization v0.17.0. The theorem references above are internal references to that manuscript. The existing 49-claim revised formal contract and its inherited original-wording boundaries are unchanged.

The accompanying Python script performs \textbf{46 exact checks}: exhaustive finite test-ring enumeration, symbolic minors and CRT identities, exact matrix calculations, and the identities behind the stable-core examples. All drawings are reproducible vector graphics. Further worked details appear on \pagerefVrange{19}{25}; the inherited revised/original claim boundary is on \pagerefV{26}. The illustrative examples are not newly certified in Lean by this guide; its finite checks are reported separately from the source release. Infinite claims are supported by the arguments given here, not by extrapolating a finite image.

