Coverage in every open normal quotient of a compact totally disconnected group
implies density of the conjugacy-saturated samples and hence the finite separator.
General arithmetic Frobenius coverage remains unformalized. the \hyperref[book:x-construction-25]{system-isomorphism and finite-cyclotomic comparison} now proves
the bridge from componentwise nonisomorphic systems to nonisomorphic members
at the selected coefficient prime, under density on the required good-place
overlaps. It also proves the complete restricted separator for a fixed finite
